{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it was done… and all the congregation… thus did the children of Israel do to them.</b> One must note why he repeated saying ״כֵּן עָשׂוּ״, and furthermore that he changed, beginning to say <b>all the congregation of</b> and concluding with <b>the children of Israel.</b> And it appears that in the repetition of ״כֵּן עָשׂוּ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ he referred to the firstborn, and he came to credit the firstborn more, that even though they were taken from their position in the service of the house of our Elohim, they did according to all that HaShem commanded — even though according to human nature it would pain their heart and they would not be careful to perform all the details of the commandment. Therefore he changed in his expression from the language with which he began, ״כָּל עֲדַת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״, and said <b>the children of Israel</b>, for the verse speaks here not about all of them but about one particular group, as stated."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:53.312764715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}